@provenance case-1 compression pilot (2026-08-12): 5 marks across 3 independent zai-1 transcripts (3813, 3815, 3816 — mechanically verified); runner-graded "what would actually have helped at the stuck moment". Clears the >=3-transcript bar independently of the debrief.
@review claude-2 2026-08-12 APPROVE. Transcript count verified, not asserted. @grade added (batch defect B1).

! conclusion:
  To prove an identity between subobjects-of-a-subobject, lift both
  sides into the ambient object with the library's lift/restrict API,
  prove the identity there where the full lattice API applies, and
  reflect the result back through injectivity of the lift.

  + context: You must show K ⊓ L = X or K ⊔ L = Y where K, L are
    subobjects reinterpreted inside another subobject (intermediate
    fields inside a fixed field, subgroups inside a subgroup). The
    sublattice's own API is thin; direct reasoning stalls on coercions.

  + IF: The library provides a lift/restrict pair with per-operation
    lemmas (lift_inf, lift_sup, lift_restrict) and an injectivity lemma
    (lift_injective) — in Mathlib for IntermediateField, at
    FieldTheory/Basic (restrict at :885, lift at :652 as of 2026-08).

  + HOWEVER: The technique needs ALL the per-operation lift lemmas to
    exist for the operations in your identity — a missing lift_sup means
    proving it yourself first. And when a DIRECT lemma for your identity
    exists (e.g. the meet/join idiom in FieldTheory/LinearDisjoint), the
    lift-reflect detour is unnecessary lattice-homomorphism work — search
    for the direct route before committing to the detour.

  + THEN: Apply lift to both sides; rewrite with the per-operation lift
    lemmas until the identity is between ambient objects; close with the
    ambient API; finish by lift_injective. Write it as an explicit calc
    chain — each step names one lift lemma.

  + BECAUSE: Injectivity reflection converts a thin-API setting into a
    rich-API setting at the cost of one lemma per operation — the
    cheapest general exit from subobject-of-subobject reasoning.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Search the namespace for the lift/restrict family by BARE name inside the defining file — qualified-name grep misses namespace declarations.]
